cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation or the accompanying note, please cite it as below."
title: "mobius-cpt: a Lean 4 formalisation of the PCT theorem for Möbius-covariant Wightman conformal field theories on the circle"
abstract: >-
  Tener (Comm. Math. Phys. 407 (2026), no. 6, paper no. 128) proves a PCT theorem for
  Möbius-covariant Wightman conformal field theories on the circle in a setting that assumes
  neither a Hilbert space nor unitarity: the boost flow of such a theory admits an analytic
  continuation to the closed strip 0 <= Im tau <= pi, and at the far edge tau = i*pi that
  continuation reverses the order of any product of fields smeared inside the upper semicircle,
  reflects each test function through z -> 1/z, and multiplies the result by (-1)^d, where d is
  the sum of the conformal dimensions. This repository contains a machine-checked formalisation
  of that theorem in Lean 4 with mathlib, covering Definition 3.1 and Lemmas 3.4, 3.6, 3.7, 3.8,
  3.9 leading to Theorem 3.10, together with the Reeh-Schlieder property for the two reference
  semicircles, which is what makes the continued operators densely defined. It also contains a
  mathematician-facing research note (Japanese body, English title and abstract) that presents
  the proof architecture as ordinary mathematics, records the formalisation status at a pinned
  revision, and sets out the points at which the published proof compresses an argument that a
  complete proof must supply. Theorem 3.10 is the analytic-continuation and order-reversal
  statement on which the PCT involution and the Bisognano-Wichmann property are subsequently
  built; those constructions are outside the scope of this formalisation.
type: software
